## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/lv.svg" width="32" alt="Latvia" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />Latvia

Latvia maintains its position as one of NATO's most institutionally integrated frontline states, continuing maximum Western alignment while broadening economic diplomacy within compatible frameworks. The country achieved a significant defense industrial milestone with the first operational deployment of domestically manufactured autonomous military drones to multiple NATO allies, demonstrating maturation from equipment importer to producer. PM Siliņa's UAE engagement with sovereign wealth fund representatives indicates expanding economic partnerships beyond traditional EU/NATO circles while maintaining zero hedging toward alternative powers. The sixth opposition no-confidence motion against the government failed with standard results, confirming routine political opposition within stable democratic institutions. Defense spending remains at 4.91% of GDP with additional 70 million euro defense industrial investment approved, sustaining the post-2022 security transformation trajectory. Coalition dynamics continue established patterns of surface instability within structurally stable governance framework as October 2026 elections approach.

**Key developments:**

- **Security:** Latvia, Estonia and Belgium became first European countries to deploy 'Blaze' autonomous interceptor drones manufactured by Latvian defense tech company Origin Robotics. Defense Minister Sprūds announced delivery as response to growing airspace threats. Latvia allocated 50 million euros for UAV capabilities in 2026, up from 20 million in previous year.
- **Economic:** Cabinet approved 40 million euro allocation for defense industry projects targeting military and dual-use manufacturing to create 280 jobs and attract 260 million total investment. Additional 30 million under consideration for expanded defense industrial capacity.
- **Diplomatic:** PM Siliņa conducted working visit to Dubai February 2-5 for World Government Summit, leading delegation with Health Minister and entrepreneurs. Met with Mubadala investment fund representatives (\$380 billion portfolio), promoted cooperation in energy, data centers, logistics. Spoke alongside Serbia's PM on national transformation.
- **Domestic:** Latvia First party submitted another resignation demand against PM Siliņa citing excessive classification of government documents. Parliament lacked quorum for vote, with 46 coalition deputies voting against and one abstaining. This marks the sixth such motion since Siliņa took office.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Latvian officials attend Milan-Cortina Olympics, showcase Baltic unity** — PM Siliņa and President Rinkēvičs attended the Winter Olympics, with Siliņa skating at training and Rinkēvičs meeting athletes and posing with Baltic counterparts. Coverage included equipment delays for Latvia's largest-ever Olympic delegation of 68 athletes. *([sports.tvnet.lv](https://sports.tvnet.lv/8411900/video-silina-slido-milanas-olimpiskaja-arena-latvijas-hokeja-izlases-trenina))*
- **President Rinkēvičs calls for investigation of Epstein files mentioning Latvia** — President Rinkēvičs said Latvian authorities should investigate information in Jeffrey Epstein files that mention Latvia as a potential location for recruiting underage girls. He noted Latvia has not yet received legal assistance requests from the US. *([tvnet.lv](https://www.tvnet.lv/8407877/tiesibsargajosajam-iestadem-jaizpeta-epstina-failos-mineta-informacija-par-latviju-uzsver-rinkevics))*
- **Rinkēvičs supports European diplomacy with Russia while calling attacks near genocide** — President Rinkēvičs said Russia's attacks on Ukraine's energy infrastructure 'practically approach genocide' while supporting the idea of a special European envoy for talks with Russia. He and Estonia's president backed European diplomatic engagement coordinated with Ukraine. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8407922/faktiski-tuvojas-genocidam-rinkevics-par-krievijas-uzbrukumiem-ukrainas-energetikas-infrastrukturai))*
- **Corruption investigation launched at two regional hospitals** — Investigators suspect officials at Ogre district hospital and Liepāja regional hospital may have caused over €300,000 in overpayments through potentially criminal actions when contracting with medical supply vendors. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8410298/kratisanas-liepajas-un-ogres-slimnicas-kas-zinams-lidz-sim))*
- **Riga municipal companies dismiss Russian and Belarusian citizens** — Multiple Russian and Belarusian citizens have been dismissed from companies owned by Riga municipality, following national policy regarding aggressor state nationals in public sector roles. *([tvnet.lv](https://tvnet.lv/8410513/ari-no-rigas-pasvaldibas-kapitalsabiedribam-atlaisti-vairaki-agresorvalstu-pilsoni))*
- **State Security Service initiates criminal case over Russian business ties** — The State Security Service (VDD) recommended prosecutors launch criminal proceedings against a Latvian resident for allegedly providing unauthorized programming services to a Russian company, violating sanctions regulations. *([lvportals.lv](https://lvportals.lv/dienaskartiba/386028-vdd-rosina-pret-personu-kriminalvajasanu-par-programmesanas-pakalpojumu-sniegsanu-uznemumam-krievija-2026))*
</Accordion>---

